-- The library half of the cross-IMPORT refusal fixture, which is
-- `export-refused.l4` beside it. This file typechecks and evaluates perfectly
-- well; it exists only to be imported.
--
-- It is deliberately outside every golden glob. Imports resolve
-- importer-relative, so the two files have to share a directory, and only one
-- of them is meant to fail -- hence `not-ok/import/*-refused.l4` in
-- jl4/tests/Main.hs rather than a whole-directory glob.

§ `Rates`
    GIVEN `the rate` IS A NUMBER TYPICALLY 0.05

GIVEN amount IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`scaled by the rate` amount MEANS amount TIMES `the rate`
